ng and doesn't want to come off  as a complaining actor  it was a huge discomfort for him while  filming and the paint even started to  wear down and break his skin  however like dave the removal process  was far worse  he also had to have a portable sauna  built just for him to d-vision  to make things better he called it his  little magical cupboard and would bring  a beer in with him to pass the time  the whole process took about three hours  and i didn't think for a minute what  that was actually gonna mean to me  physically karen gillen's days on  guardians of the galaxy  started at 2 am because of her 4 hour  painting process  once the prosthetics were assembled on  her face properly the artists  spent hours making sure every part of  exposed skin matched the blue of her  prosthetics  on top of all the paint they also  airbrushed her with another layer  just to make sure they had everything  covered  another 30 minutes was needed at the end  of the day to get all that paint off  karen described it as claustrophobic but  when it was all said and done it really  helped her get into character  just like her on-screen sister zoe  saldana was on set bright and early  while filming guardians of the galaxy  it sucks to have to wake up at 2 30 in  the morning and by the time we started  shooting you feel like you've already  lived half a day  becoming gamora was done using green  airbrushed paint  and some colored facial makeup it needed  to be put onto any area of her body that  wasn't covered by her costume  listen to her talk about how brutal it  was  the whole coming together of gamora  every morning  that was a little grueling the science  of the 1930s was not in favor of buddy  ebsen when he took on the role of tin  man in the wizard of oz  he was painted head to toe in metallic  paint  that sent him to the hospital with lung  failure he was then recast by jack haley  who was instead  transformed by the paste version of the  paint however it left  jack with an eye infection and out of  commission for a week of filming  believe it or not rafe finds his  voldemort costume was mostly white paint  he'd spend hours in the makeup chair  each morning making sure his face was  evenly painted the paint was also used  to make his skin look translucent  and to draw on the delicate lines on his  face and scalp  although it took over three hours rafe's  treacherous time in the makeup  department paid off  even the child actors were terrified of  him and you  shall be dead gemma chan is thinking  twice about ever taking another role  where they need to paint her body  it's all thanks to the process she had  to endure while becoming  minerva in captain marvel she was on set  every day at 2 45 am  where she would spend 4 hours getting  airbrushed that was challenging  i didn't really think it through when i  said yes to playing a blue character  i'd think twice about it again by the  end of the film the makeup was even  starting to irritate her skin  congratulations for michael rooker being  yondu meant having  six layers of paint airbrushed on him  every day  he would have to get on set so early for  the three-hour process that he just  started sleeping right in the makeup  chair  he soon realized that others like zoe  saldana and dave bautista had to go  through an even worse process than  himself  and it eventually started to get easier  but the whole ordeal was still  tough you just gotta let it go you can't  fight it right  johnny depp dove right into the process  of becoming the mad hatter and  loved putting together the character but  that doesn't mean the paint application  was enjoyable  his character was done up using almost  entirely airbrushed paint  based on tim burton's concept drawings  the process did take hours but  johnny knew it was all for the greater  purpose of making sure his character was  the best it could be  we've all heard how intense heath  ledger's transformation was for the  joker  his face was covered in actual paint  while it was drying he was asked to  scrunch his face in order to give the  effective lines  the makeup process only took about an  hour however the grueling process came  while trying to perfect the imperfect  look  it took weeks of trial and error for  heath and his makeup artist  jim carrey's makeup process involved  prosthetics and a whole lot of green  paint on his face  neck and head it took jim carrey four  hours to get camera ready each day  the painting was so gruesome and long  that it caused jim carrey to become  irritated  and short-tempered with the rest of the  cast and crew  apparently it drove the actor insane  spoken  like her counterpart the tin man the  wizard of oz wicked witch actress  margaret hamilton was sent to the  hospital because of the paint used on  her  not only did the copper-based green  liquid cause intense skin reactions  but its elements also made her more  flammable and while working with fire  props she burned her face and hands  really badly michael keaton's makeup  in beetlejuice might just look like it  was splashed on but  very deliberate painting went into  making him look just as tim burton  wanted him to  his face was painted using a mixture of  yellow and white  and his eye circles were created using  brown and purple paints  michael says after a day of makeup and  rabid acting he went home  beat and exhausted ron pearlman's  hellboy transformation was a four  hour long adventure his entire body was  painted by hand including the  prosthetics  by his makeup artist jake garber it was  so  long that jake needed to make sure ron  had breaks in between to make the  grueling process  more bearable days where hellboy had his  shirt off took even more time  to get through it ron would tell himself  there are a million guys that wish they  were you right now  and there's absolutely no reason you  should ever complain  these transformations brought a level of  realness to the big screen that just  couldn't have been replicated with  visual effects the paint  literally becomes a part of the  character however it was at the expense  of the actors having  a brutal experience do you think there  was a way to make these celebs  experiences  a bit better thanks for watching

